// The entry points for the two checks of a `then` node that name something to
// read: a check function (then_fn, which goes on to its signature and value,
// sig.id and value.id) and an export (fit_then_imp, `then (import NAME):(value)`
// and `then (import NAME)[i]:(value)`). fit_then_kind (../dispatch.id) calls
// then_fn itself and routes the export's kind here.

// An export read after the call: held to what an `(import NAME)` argument is
// (fit_import, ../../read/impcheck.id: a `given`, an owner that setup reaches),
// unless the function under test reaches the owner itself -- the call sets the
// export, and a `given` of the owner would run it twice before the check
// instead of once, so what the check finds could differ from what one call
// leaves; a call that does not set it at run time traps as an uninitialised
// export. It may not read back what that call only declared (chk_own_import,
// ../../more/flag/reqtests.id). Then its fields, index and value (then_imp_field,
// ./sig.id).
fit_then_imp(int chk_node) {
  int ci = (import ni1)[chk_node];
  string imp_nm = (import ns1)[chk_node];
  int ek = find_str((import enames), imp_nm);
} chain (int chk_node) {
  string want = "";
  if(ek >= 0) {
    want = (import etypes)[ek];
  }
  if(ek < 0 || reaches((import ns1)[((import casefn)[ci])], (import eowners)[ek]) == 0) {
    fit_import(ci, chk_node, want);
  }
} chain (int chk_node) {
  chk_own_import(ci, chk_node);
  if(ek >= 0) {
    then_imp_field(ci, chk_node, want);
  }
} return void;
